1️⃣ From scratch, how will you create infrastructure?

"When I create infrastructure from scratch, I start with networking first.
I design the VPC with CIDR planning, then create public and private subnets across multiple AZs.

After that, I configure Internet Gateway, NAT Gateway, and route tables.

Next, I set up security — security groups, NACLs, IAM roles and policies.

Once the base network is ready, I provision compute like EC2 or EKS, then storage like S3 and RDS.

Finally, I configure monitoring, logging, and CI/CD access.

I automate everything using Terraform so the infra is repeatable and version-controlled"
